{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Therefore the children of Israel do not eat.</b> In remembrance of the miracle, that Jacob was saved from the angel, who touched only the hollow of his thigh and did not kill him — like a person who constantly feels an ailment in his head or his heart, and takes upon himself not to eat of the head or the heart anymore, so that it serve as a remedy. Another explanation: because the children of Israel did improperly, for they let him go alone and did not provide him with an escort, and he was harmed through them in the gid hanasheh — therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, forbade the gid hanasheh to them, so that they would be careful in the mitzvah of escort from then on. And therefore Jacob was careful to escort his son Joseph when he sent him to his brothers."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:27.006101636Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}